# Linked git worktrees checked out inside the repo. A worktree is a second copy
# of this tree, so without these `prettier --check .` walks the whole project
# twice — and reports the *other* checkout's generated Convex client, which the
# `convex/_generated/` line above cannot match because it is anchored to the
# root. That made `npm run format:check` fail locally no matter what was
# written, which is how formatting slips got as far as CI: a check that always
# fails is a check nobody runs.
